      ],
      "id": "9xwsn3g"
    },
    {
      "id": "5v1qna3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The interior of the Earth is divided into three primary layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "The crust comprises two distinct types: Continental Crust (thicker, granitic) and Oceanic Crust (thinner, basaltic).",
        "The upper portion of the mantle includes the Asthenosphere, which serves as the primary source of magma.",
        "The Earth's core is subdivided into a liquid outer core and a solid inner core composed primarily of Nickel and Iron (NIFE).",
        "Seismic discontinuities mark sharp compositional and physical state changes at boundary layers within the Earth."
      ],
      "id": "7azpl2i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nma3ecj",
      "content": "• Average radius of Earth: about 6371 km."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uphs745",
      "content": "• Earth's interior temperature increases with depth (geothermal gradient)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "159dlq3",
      "content": "• Density also increases toward the center."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t489nei",
      "content": "• The Earth is composed mainly of iron, oxygen, silicon, magnesium and nickel."
    },
    {
      "id": "qu44aio",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Sources of Information about the Earth's Interior"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a41s6ma",
      "content": "A. Direct Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pxaantm",
      "content": "• Mining and deep drilling projects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5iv192e",
      "content": "• Volcanic eruptions bring materials from inside the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8j98gbn",
      "content": "B. Indirect Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ity4hyz",
      "content": "• Seismic waves produced by earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mugmu59",
      "content": "• Gravitational force studies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "camtp5v",
      "content": "• Magnetic field observations."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9d33gz6",
      "content": "• Meteorite composition which is similar to Earth's interior."
    },
    {
      "id": "w9x0zu9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Major Layers of the Earth"
    },
    {
